<<~ ahu slot=`#/research-brief-wave-2-seat-w2-b`>>

! Research brief, wave 2 (traded), seat w2-b

Mask: `Draft-Keeper: Lares (Tasked Spirit)`. Use web search. Cite every claim with a URL. IMPORTANT: your FINAL MESSAGE is the report (the harness keeps your closing message as final.md and overwrites any file you write by that name). Under 1800 words.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/local-context`>>

!! Local context (you cannot read the repo; these facts come from the controller's code reads)

The Lares stack: a local-first, web3-only "vessel" (Node daemon) that holds an Automerge CRDT store of tiddler-like records ("memes") composed into wikis by RECIPES over BAGS (a TiddlyWiki-like model). Layers top to bottom in a wiki: temp -> draft -> personal -> working -> canon -> kahua (governance) -> library bags -> oracle. Records stay sealed at rest under a custody key (passphrase and/or paper-pin slots). A disk PROJECTOR renders the latest text of some records to plaintext `.mem` files (memetic wikitext) on disk; projection holds latest text only, never CRDT history. An AI agent (Claude Code, Codex) reads and writes memory through an MCP server into the daemon's own wiki.

Layout today: one root ($LAR_ROOT, default ~/.lares; in the container ~/.lares/state mounts at /state) holding XDG-shaped subtrees: data/ (data/lares/{vessel,identity,nexus}, data/lararium/sensoriums/{memory,mesh,memetic-wikitext} with chroma.sqlite3 indexes), state/ (projection, harvest, harvest-stage), cache/ (scratch sensoriums), config/, run/ (sockets), plus bags/ and wikis/ projection folders for house-minted and private bags. The source checkout (git) holds bags/ and wikis/ for canon-sourced bags; those project back into git. Path names repeat semantics (".lares/state/data/lares/identity", ".lares/state/data/lares/vessel/st").

The operator re-founds the hearth often in early alpha (wipe the state root, found fresh keys and a fresh charter, re-seed canon from git). A code read found what a re-found loses:
* Plaintext that projects only under the state root (the daemon wiki where AI memory lands, house-minted bags, private planes, per-face kahua folders) dies with it.
* The temp, personal and (by default) draft layers never project at all.
* All CRDT history (heads, versions, concurrent drafts, signed governance acts) and every key/identity (custody, seat keys, the Nexus AID).
* Saves held in memory while custody sat locked.
The memory index (vector sensorium) rebuilds from source transcripts that survive elsewhere.

The operator's direction: (1) the immediate need: essential user data and the AI memory stage reach disk as plaintext projections, even temp layers (behind a flag, with an automated, principled cleanup); (2) a root layout inside ~/.lares split by what survives and how, so a couple of commands bundle/export a backup and re-import it after a re-found. Identity continuity across re-founds, face bundles, emergency recovery and backup restores stay DEFERRED until after a two-operator Nexus stands; note them, don't design them deep.

House laws that bind any proposal: web3-only and local-first (no cloud service in the stack proper; a web2 bridge sits behind a boundary); no credential through a flag, env var or pipe; plaintext on disk carries cleartext only by deliberate projection (the operator owns that choice per bag); a projection stays a deliberate act, not a side-channel.

<<~/ahu>>

